From: Christian Kündig <christian@kuendig.info>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep the host FS base until pthread_teb is initialized.

The GE syscall-user-dispatch patch sequence reverts Valve's
ntdll-Syscall_Emulation and drops its non-null pthread_teb check in
init_handler(). If a signal arrives before init_syscall_frame() has saved
the host TEB, ARCH_SET_FS with a null base clears the live host TLS base.
save_context() then calls NtCurrentTeb(), implemented on the Unix side
with pthread_getspecific(), which needs that TLS base.

Restore the guard without changing the preceding SUD ALLOW transition.
This is a candidate for Asylum's BmLauncher crash in pthread_getspecific
while segv_handler saves the context. The original fault and the value of
pthread_teb have not yet been recovered from its root-owned core, so the
candidate still needs a Deck comparison against the unmodified -next.

Co-Authored-By: Codex GPT-6.1 Sol <noreply@openai.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -928,7 +928,8 @@ static inline ucontext_t *init_handler( void *sigcontext )
     {
         struct amd64_thread_data *thread_data = (struct amd64_thread_data *)&get_current_teb()->GdiTebBatch;
         thread_data->syscall_dispatch = 0; /* SYSCALL_DISPATCH_FILTER_ALLOW */
-        if (fs32_sel) arch_prctl( ARCH_SET_FS, thread_data->pthread_teb );
+        if (fs32_sel && thread_data->pthread_teb)
+            arch_prctl( ARCH_SET_FS, thread_data->pthread_teb );
     }
 #elif defined __APPLE__
     {
